        "a": "Logistic regression: predicts probability of binary outcome (buy/not buy). Works: linear combination of features passed through sigmoid (outputs 0-1 probability). Interpretation: coefficient sign indicates feature effect (positive=more likely to buy). Step 1-Label: past 7 days, who bought? Buy=1, no=0. Step 2-Features: browsing time, items viewed, cart adds, email opens, account age, device, geography, prior purchase history, price range viewed. Start simple, add gradually. Step 3-Feature engineering: interaction terms (email_opens×browsing_time), bins (new vs returning), recency (days since last purchase). Step 4-Split: 70% train, 30% test. Step 5-Train: fit logistic regression. Step 6-Evaluate: accuracy, precision, recall, ROC-AUC. Step 7-Interpret: logistic_odds=e^(coefficient). If coefficient=0.5, odds ratio=1.65 (1.65x more likely per unit increase). Step 8-Threshold: default 0.5 probability=buy. Adjust if false positives/negatives cost differently. Step 9-Predict: score all users, rank by purchase probability, target top 20%. Real: email campaign. Score users, send to top 10% (highest probability). Expected 15% conversion vs baseline 8%. ROI positive if cost_per_email<(revenue_per_purchase×lift)."
