        "a": "def knn(X_train, y_train, X_test, k): predictions=[]; for test_point in X_test: distances=[(euclidean_distance(test_point, train_point), label) for train_point, label in zip(X_train, y_train)]; distances.sort(); neighbors=[label for _, label in distances[:k]]; predictions.append(majority_vote(neighbors)). Euclidean: sqrt(Σ(x_i-y_i)²). Choosing K: (1) Odd K avoids ties. (2) Validation curve: CV error vs K, find elbow. (3) Rule: K~sqrt(n). (4) Domain: larger K→smoother, underfitting. Smaller K→noisy, overfitting. (5) Practical: k=3-10 typical. Example: k=1 overfits, k=n underfits. Cross-validation: pick k with lowest CV error. KNN simple but slow (O(n) per prediction)."
