        "domain": "general",
        "a": "D>>n regime causes: (1) Distance meaningless (all equally far). (2) Sparse data, few samples in middle. (3) Overfitting (many parameters, fit noise). (4) Slow training, high memory. Solutions: (1) Feature reduction-PCA to 50 components (keeps 95% variance, 10x speedup). (2) Feature selection-filter (correlation, MI), wrapper (backward elimination), embedded (Lasso). Keep top 20 features. (3) Domain knowledge-engineer domain-specific features (10 features). (4) Regularization-L1/L2 (Lasso zeros weak features). (5) Tree-based-XGBoost handles high-D, picks important features. Real: genomics 20K genes, 100 patients. Cannot train without reduction. PCA→100 components. Train classifier on reduced. Speed 100x faster, accuracy improved (less overfitting). Modern: deep learning embeds high-D (learns useful projection). Best: start with reduction (PCA or selection), then model."
